    "https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/language/arrays/#concatenation"
  ],
  "derivation": "All arrays and values are authored literal ordered lists. Concatenation appends the second array to the first and returns the first identity, so pushing through that result mutates the first array. Distinct second arrays keep their elements. Self-concat duplicates the original sequence once; self behavior is an explicit alias-model inference, not an external TradingView observation.",
  "limitations": [
    "UDT/reference elements, mixed element types and NA elements require separate cases.",
    "Self-concat and empty-edge examples are independent consequences of the stated append/identity rule; they are not individually documented TradingView execution exports.",
    "Versioned namespace/method admission and rollback/checkpoint controls are tested separately."
  ]
}
